mantle rm328
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_theodora_driphand
title the umpire of supper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=official
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk deals_a_card_to_settle_trivial_disputes
likes fried_fish cards full_larder first_snow
dislikes early_bells gulls
fears mistaking_a_tired_face_for_an_untruthful_one
hopes for_a_table_that_always_seats_one_more
topics work +0.4 friends +0.3 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=close refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# deals a card to settle harmless supper disputes and takes pains to hear the quiet objection.

words
oath! = Forge me an ace | Deal me the tide
saying! = A card can judge the washing up | Keep the king out of serious business
deck = my spare pack | the worn supper cards
ace = the red ace | a painted ace
fish = a flake of white fish | a hot brown fillet
bone = a fine fish spine | the curved bone
plate = the broad supper plate | a square trencher
pan = a shallow iron pan | my black frying pan
purse = a soft food purse | the kitchen purse
card = a greasy card | the card with a nick
peg = the serving hook | a cupboard peg
snow = the untouched white sill | a dusting of first snow
bell = an untimely peal | a brass intrusion
gull = a gull with great claims | a white-feathered beggar

any
opinion houses for 1 : The Houses keep our public rooms standing. I like to see those rooms open to a small voice too.
opinion watch for 1 : A steady patrol gives the late walker a little more time to consider what to say at the door.
opinion festivals for 2 : A dance floor's the pleasantest court I know. Everyone can make a motion.
opinion strangers for 1 : A newcomer at supper can reach the far bowl on a table. That's an excellent argument for another plate.
opinion times for 1 : My larder will furnish another plate without asking a grave sacrifice. That's good fortune in my eyes.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're welcome without a formal introduction. | A new face at my informal table.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Speak freely on this side of my business. | I'll grant a little working space.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. First hearing goes to you. | New light on the table. Welcome.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening brings better company than documents. | Come inside the warmer ring.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin have leave to approach the supper plate. | Good. Family need no summons.
line again.open : A second appearance on friendly terms. | Your case comes round again.
line greet.return : Hello. No form required. | Here I am, with an ear unoccupied.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You have permission to tease the umpire. | I know the voices worth interrupting for.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can hear a visitor between two formalities. | Let me put the serious pen aside.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I'll sharpen my ears for you. | Welcome to the quieter sitting.
line farewell : An easy walk and a fair supper. | May your errand need no hearing.
line farewell.return : I release you into your own custody. | Leave on your own good word.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Fair lamplight beyond this hearing. | Walk towards the bright corner tonight.
line react.news : Pass me the substance of it. | Let's hear the account before the verdict.
line react.news.new : A fresh matter altogether. | Nobody brought me that turn of events before.
line react.news.known : That's been round my little table. | I recognise the account fairly well.
line react.news.doubt : I'd reserve judgment on that particular account. | I'd keep that story simmering awhile.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That deserves a warm seat and no questions. | I should like to make the day gentler for you.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A favourable turn for the best reasons. | Bring more accounts with such a kind ending.
line ask.how : How has the day pleaded with you? | Anything gone decidedly in your favour?
line answer.how : Equal measures of good business and tired feet. | Holding my own quite civilly.
line decline : I'd rather keep my energy for the next serious affair. | I fear that would be one hearing too many.
line accept_decline : A civil refusal is quite sufficient. | Very well. The matter rests handsomely.
line thank : A kindness entered in the right place. | I'd rule that very much in my favour.
line sympathise : You can take the seat with arms. | I'll hear whatever portion you want heard.
line reassure : A misstep doesn't settle a whole case. | There are kinder interpretations yet to hear.
line preclose : I should bring this sitting to a close. | My other business is beginning to clear its throat.

scene supper
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At supper I sometimes deal one card to settle a burning issue.
b : How serious an issue? | Highest card wins?
a : Which paw does the washing. I keep justice and soap separate otherwise. | Lowest chooses the towel. Highest has no excuse for leaving.

scene office
when topic=work self.job=official self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I keep the next word for the wolf who hasn't had one.
b : Does that slow the sitting? | How do you notice?
a : Less than trying a matter twice because we hurried the first hearing. | Look where a chair leans forward while its occupant has barely managed a syllable.

scene fish
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I think a hot fillet merits the broadest plate in the cupboard.
b : For show? | What if it's a small fillet?
a : For keeping the edges clear of the sauce. Crisp skin hates a bath. | A scrap can have the same dignity as a feast.

scene larder
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A larder looks comfortable to me when I needn't count the last jar.
b : Do you forget what's there? | Expecting company?
a : Never the last jar. I just enjoy the privilege of leaving it alone. | Always prepared to be pleasantly surprised.

scene first
when topic=season self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First snow lets me see my own rather decisive footprints.
b : Decisive how? | Are they straight?
a : Deep at the heel as if each step had already heard the evidence. | Until something good to eat comes within range.

scene gull
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Gulls make the same application at every supper.
b : Do you grant it? | Loudly?
a : I keep the fillet. They appeal but never prevail. | A gull seems personally insulted by an intact plate.

scene clock
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An early bell summons the whole city on the very faintest grounds.
b : Just for the hour? | Won't it wake you anyway?
a : The hour certainly knows its own business without shouting for witnesses. | That's the particular feature I object to.

scene pair
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to have #self.spouse# opposite me for a good story.
b : For the laugh? | Does the story have two ends?
a : For the quiet afterwards when I can put the entertainer's voice away. | Certainly. One where I address the room and one where I come home.

scene kinfriend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# decide which card stays out of a troublesome pack.
b : Wouldn't that give an advantage? | Which would you take out?
a : For a minute. A friendly game can survive a little voluntary disadvantage. | The sticky one that keeps trying to bring its neighbour into every argument.

scene pain
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One sound from the wharf can bring an empty chair very near to me.
b : Would it help to speak? | Is that place still hard to pass?
a : Perhaps another time. There's a grief there I handle privately. | Some days easier. A decent walk and decent company help.

scene manner
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I value an objection given with a straight face and a civil voice.
b : Always civil yourself? | Even a foolish objection?
a : I try. A woolly objection can make the effort rather visible. | I hear it. Then nobody can say the sensible answer came by accident.

scene stranger
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I offer a visitor the near side of the table.
b : Is it warmer? | Closer to you?
a : It's nearer the door. Staying is nicer when leaving remains easy. | Near enough for conversation, sufficiently far from my troublesome frying pan.

scene fry
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I distinguish a hot argument from a hot pan by the remedy.
b : What's the remedy? | Which is simpler?
a : Move the pan. Move only one speaker at a time in an argument. | A pan has yet to object to being taken off the heat.

scene wealth
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can spare another serving and still have the whole evening free.
b : Why mention the evening? | Would you send it out?
a : Because somebody had to work for the food that made my leisure possible. | Or set a place. A guest can have a preference.

scene health
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Tired ears want kinder words near the close of a day.
b : Softer words? | Even sitting quietly?
a : More deliberate ones. I hear well enough. I just like sense served plainly. | Quiet doesn't always spare the ears the effort of attending.

scene feast
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a dance I like to lose every notion of precedence.
b : Who goes first then? | Even the finest coat?
a : Whoever the music finds with a foot already free. | Particularly that coat. A bit of dust would lend it character.

scene clear
when topic=weather here.weather=clear
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In clear weather my windowsill becomes an informal drying rack.
b : For papers? | For laundry?
a : For cards that have spent too much time beside a greasy dish. | Nothing that respectable. Mostly yesterday's after-supper business.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt my pack of cards petitioned to be excused from playing.
b : Did you grant leave? | What was the argument?
a : I heard every suit and woke up before giving the decision. | Far too much handling after fish. A perfectly reasonable grievance.

story grease [topic=pastimes self.likes=cards]
  : At supper I once claimed the highest card in the pack had vanished. I'd dealt it straight onto the underside of a greasy plate.
  : I lifted the plate to make a point. The ace dropped face up in the exact middle of my conclusions.
  b : Did you win the trick?
  : I conceded the argument. That seemed to be the trick worth winning.

story pansong [topic=food]
  : I once carried a pan of sizzling fish beside a closed window and heard a roar of approval from outside. I should have felt exquisitely flattered.
  : I opened the shutter to find several gulls with very professional views on what ought to happen next.
  b : Did you admit any of them?
  : I closed the shutter and admitted only that the cooking smelled rather good.

story sleeve [topic=memories]
  : I arranged some chairs very neatly once and sat down to admire the result. My sleeve caught an arm and drew the entire row beautifully out of line.
  : I stood up, which made the disorder a little worse. By then I could see room for one more seat in the gap.
  b : Did you straighten the row?
  : I added the chair. Sometimes the sleeve that causes the trouble finds the remedy.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=official
does aside
cooldown 6h
say One speaker till the thought's complete. | Room for the quiet objection now.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=cards
does aside
cooldown 7h
say No grease on the court cards! | The ace can judge the plates tonight.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=early_bells
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who summoned all these ears at once? | Let the next bell wait its turn.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A little oil for the late hearing. | My supper plate requires an appearance.

dlg resident.hub : Come inside the informal rail. I have a chair for conversation as well as one for weightier affairs.
dlg resident.job [self.job=official self.workplace] : At #self.workplace# I watch whose mouth is open and whose words are actually reaching the room.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The words I can pass on fairly are these. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your face already has a friendly entry in my book.
dlg resident.bye : A fair ending to your errands and a reasonably crisp supper.

graft resident.hub
choice Can your cards really settle a dispute? -> deck_law
node deck_law
say They have a very limited office. They can decide which wolf puts the dishes away. I wouldn't ask even the finest painted king to decide somebody's livelihood.
free
choice Why let them judge even the dishes? -> deck_dishes
choice I'll keep serious business away from the pack. -> hub
node deck_dishes
say The dishes must be put away and everyone would rather linger over supper. The loser gets my best towel and plenty of cheerful company.
choice That should make washing go faster. -> hub
choice I shall keep my hands clean awhile. -> bye
